### 2. Bug Code Snippet Analysis & Bug Location

**Key code section:**
```js
this.postExecuted([ 'shape.toggleCollapse' ], LOW_PRIORITY, function(e) {
  var shape = e.context.shape,
      defaultSize = elementFactory._getDefaultSize(shape),
      newBounds;

  if (shape.collapsed) {

    // resize to default size of collapsed shapes
    newBounds = collapsedBounds(shape, defaultSize);
  } else {

    // resize to bounds of max(visible children, defaultSize)
    newBounds = expandedBounds(shape, defaultSize);
  }

  modeling.resizeShape(shape, newBounds, null, {
    autoResize: shape.collapsed ? false : 'nwse'
  });
});
```
- The code always recalculates the bounds and resizes the shape after a collapse/expand toggle.
- If the shape is already collapsed and its size is already the default, this will still forcibly resize it, which can cause issues if the shape's size was already correct or if another property (like Ad Hoc) was toggled.

**Potential Fix:**  
Only resize the shape to the default collapsed size if it is not already at that size. This prevents unnecessary resizing and dimension changes when toggling properties like Ad Hoc on an already-collapsed subprocess.

